                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b6b23f26-739e-3fc5-98c5-5d9dba4cd61c",
                        "entry_id": "6b11a382-da1a-36d3-af62-e0363a68b2bb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Erste Entstehung der Sprache"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6aa27b2e-9d4b-4647-8729-16a4bf1d160b",
                                "sense_id": "b6b23f26-739e-3fc5-98c5-5d9dba4cd61c",
                                "text": "Es gibt mehrere Theorien darüber, wie der Sprachursprung vor sich ging."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "518c4697-82c1-4bf4-9eff-f75ef583f06b",
                                "sense_id": "b6b23f26-739e-3fc5-98c5-5d9dba4cd61c",
                                "text": "Es ist umstritten, ob es nur einen Sprachursprung (Monogenese) oder mehrere Sprachursprünge unabhängig voneinander (Polygenese) gegeben hat."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "92b15b06-3d1e-4595-9452-2571992bf204",
                                "sense_id": "b6b23f26-739e-3fc5-98c5-5d9dba4cd61c",
                                "text": "„Die Frage des Sprachursprungs ist eines der meistdiskutierten Themen in der Sprachwissenschaft des 17. und 18. Jahrhunderts. Sie begegnet in zwei Varianten: als Diskussion über den Ursprung der Sprache schlechthin und als Diskussion über den Ursprung und die Geschichte des Deutschen.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3adaeb03-c249-4530-b6cf-e9c9e6474c76",
                        "source_entry_id": "6b11a382-da1a-36d3-af62-e0363a68b2bb",
                        "source_sense_id": "b6b23f26-739e-3fc5-98c5-5d9dba4cd61c",
                        "source_sense_description": "Linguistik: Erste Entstehung der Sprache",
                        "target_lang_word": "glottogony",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "glottogony",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "41eb98c9-65ec-3a6e-bc12-4902b475d3b5",
                                        "entry_id": "00e63bd5-827c-3a4b-85cb-7b57061541ee",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The genesis of language, i. e. the emergence of a system of verbal communication from proto-linguistic or non-linguistic means of communication."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9c4d0edd-7123-3778-a6b5-6355069b4af5",
                                        "entry_id": "00e63bd5-827c-3a4b-85cb-7b57061541ee",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The study of language origins."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c70c52fe-a3a2-4e70-8673-156d471e458f",
                                                "sense_id": "9c4d0edd-7123-3778-a6b5-6355069b4af5",
                                                "text": "The origin of words is a question that now falls within the chapter of “glottogony”, resurrected after decades of inactivity. There are now quite a few glottogonic theories, some of which are also concerned with the origin of words as, for example, the one that argues that original words are connected with phonosymbolism, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1df33233-4e74-4af7-9a84-87587d45f878",
                                                "sense_id": "9c4d0edd-7123-3778-a6b5-6355069b4af5",
                                                "text": "The topic of glottogony has long been a taboo in linguistics, for the very good reason that it attracts boundless speculation: when Darwinism was freshly en vogue in the 1860s, linguistic debate was inundated with such proposals to the point where, in 1866, the Linguistic Society of Paris banned the entire topic as a hopeless exercise […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
